# Cost-controlled agent workflow

## Task shape

- Always prefer **scoped tasks** with explicit files and acceptance criteria.
- Read relevant docs (`AGENTS.md`, `docs/PROJECT_OPERATING_RULES.md`, topic specs) before coding.
- Ask for scope **only when truly blocked** — not to re-debate defined handoffs.

## Tooling

| Action | When |
|--------|------|
| `npm run build` | Code or config changed |
| `npm run qa:screens` | UI changed or explicitly requested |
| `npx playwright install chromium` | Only if QA run fails for missing browser |
| `npm install` / new deps | Only with justification |
| Broad refactors | Only when explicitly requested |

## Docs-only work

- No build required if only docs, rules, or markdown changed.
- Do not touch `public/qa/latest/` generated assets.

## Commits

- Commit and push **only when requested** or when the prompt explicitly asks.
- Code commits: build must pass; include QA assets only if QA was run for UI changes.
- Use repository commit message style; do not amend unless rules allow.

## Final report (keep short)

- Changed files
- What changed
- Build status (or “skipped — docs only”)
- QA status (if run)
- Commit hash (if committed)
